{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Session - Okta User Sessions Started from Different Countries [table]",
	"Description": "Finds accounts that successfully started sessions from more than one country inside the search window. Two countries in fifteen minutes is not travel; it is either a VPN the user turned on, or two people using the same credentials.\n\nCountries come from Okta's own client.geographicalContext, which Okta resolves at the edge at request time, falling back to the maxmind resource from the Gravwell Network Enrichment kit for events that arrive without it.  The geoSource field on each event says which was used.\n\nThreshold: 2 or more distinct countries per account. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_okta_user_sessions_started_from_different_geolocations/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_okta_user_sessions_started_from_different_geolocations.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "ea6ec421-708a-5714-980a-e233f5da2135",
	"SearchReference": "0688b6b7-1bf0-5181-93b5-9c28513a405d"
}